s Republican by about ten points, and the political environment this year favors the GOP.\n\nEvery major race rater calls the seat Safe or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a 7% chance. McKinney has raised nearly $1 million and benefits from over $2 million in outside support, while Duresky has raised under $200,000 with no outside spending. The forecast expects a Republican win by a double-digit margin, with modest uncertainty given the absence of general-election polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0491, "margin": -10.71}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0556, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0348, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0347, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0403, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0335, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0317, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0634, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0633, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0272, "margin": -14.0}]}